                "senderName": "NWS Tiyan GU",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 17 at 5:01AM ChST until October 18 at 4:00PM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Guam, Rota, Saipan and Tinian.\n\n* WHEN...Through Sunday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas. Storm drains\nand ditches may become clogged with debris. Extensive street\nflooding and flooding of creeks and rivers are possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Tropical Storm Champi (29W) will drop copious amounts of rain\nover Sunday and Monday...although an unexpected southward shift\nin track will reduce these somewhat. Tinian and Saipan will see\naround 4 to 6 inches, Rota could receive 10 to 15 inches, and\nGuam might get 12 to 20 inches.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
